starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2014-05-26T02:59:44Z","label":{"name":"documentation","color":"FFFFFF"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/44154798","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/3565#issuecomment-44154798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/3565","id":44154798,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTU0Nzk4","user":{"login":"rhelms","id":815879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/815879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms","html_url":"https://github.com/rhelms","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-05-26T03:29:20Z","updated_at":"2014-05-26T03:29:20Z","body":"For my use case, I'd rather be calling the action. When doing JSON or XML REST, the current actions work great.  \n\nHowever, to set up a SoapServer, I've got a SoapController, and an index action that sets up the SoapServer and handles the request.  The plain old PHP object handles the request, and I'd like this to call CakePHP functions to populate the response.\n\nThe existing actions seem like the best place, and moving all the CRUD actions into a component doesn't seem like what components are used for.  Either way, I'd still need to call something like requestAction, because the POPO isn't CakePHP aware, and setting up everything to call a CakePHP component from a POPO seems like unnecessary work.  I had actually started doing a similar thing just to call a Controller action, via the dispatcher, when I realised that requestAction does exactly that.\n\nI'm playing with wrapper document/literal SOAP at the moment, so if I can get the SoapServer to accept a string response consisting of rendered XML, that might come in handy anyway.\n\nI'll make a note if this as an issue in the docs repo, and if I can think of an appropriate alternate method to replace what the doco has, I'll submit a pull request.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/44154798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rhelms","id":815879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/815879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms","html_url":"https://github.com/rhelms","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhelms/subscriptions","organizati